export const BILL_REDACT_HTML = "<h3>How to Redact Your Bill (5 Minutes)</h3>\n<p><strong>The rule:</strong> Hide anything that identifies your account or your internal projects. Keep anything that shows what you used and what it cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Hide:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Organization IDs, account IDs and workspace IDs</li>\n<li>API keys and key names (even partial keys)</li>\n<li>Billing account numbers, invoice numbers and payment details</li>\n<li>Project names, app names and team names that reveal what you are building</li>\n<li>Names and emails of people on your team</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Keep:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model names (for example, the specific model and version)</li>\n<li>Input, output and cached token counts</li>\n<li>Request counts</li>\n<li>Cost per line and totals</li>\n<li>Dates or date ranges</li>\n<li>Generic labels in place of project names (Project A, Project B)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> A usage export (CSV) is more useful than a PDF invoice. If you can, send 2 to 3 months so we can see the trend.</p>\n<h4>OpenAI</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Sign in to your OpenAI platform dashboard and open the <strong>Usage</strong> page. Set the date range to the last 1 to 3 months.</li>\n<li>Export usage as CSV if available. If not, take screenshots of usage by model.</li>\n<li>In the file, delete or blank out columns for <strong>organization ID, project ID, API key ID and user</strong>.</li>\n<li>Rename project names to Project A, Project B, and so on.</li>\n<li>Keep the <strong>model, token counts (input, output, cached), request counts and cost</strong> columns.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>Anthropic</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Sign in to the Anthropic Console and open the <strong>Usage</strong> or <strong>Cost</strong> view. Set the range to the last 1 to 3 months.</li>\n<li>Export as CSV if available, or take screenshots grouped by model.</li>\n<li>Remove <strong>organization ID, workspace names, API key names and any user emails</strong>.</li>\n<li>Keep the <strong>model, input and output tokens, cache read and cache write tokens, and cost</strong>.</li>\n<li>If cache columns show zero, leave them in. That tells us a lot.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>Cursor</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Open your Cursor team or account dashboard and go to the <strong>Usage</strong> or <strong>Billing</strong> section.</li>\n<li>Export or screenshot usage by model and by period.</li>\n<li>Remove <strong>team name, member names and emails, and any account or invoice numbers</strong>.</li>\n<li>If usage is shown per member, replace names with Dev 1, Dev 2, and so on.</li>\n<li>Keep the <strong>model, request or token counts, and cost per period</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>AWS Bedrock</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>In the AWS console, open <strong>Cost Explorer</strong>. Filter <strong>Service = Amazon Bedrock</strong>. Group by <strong>Usage type</strong> (and by model if available). Set the range to the last 1 to 3 months.</li>\n<li>Download the CSV.</li>\n<li>Remove <strong>AWS account IDs, linked account names, resource ARNs and cost allocation tags</strong> that name projects.</li>\n<li>Do not send IAM details, access keys or console screenshots that show your account menu.</li>\n<li>Keep <strong>usage type, model, region, input and output token usage, and cost</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Not sure you redacted enough?</strong> Send it with your notes and say so. If we spot anything that should not be there, we delete the file and ask you to resend.</p>\n";
export const BILL_FAQ_HTML = "<h3>FAQ</h3>\n<details><summary>Is this secure?</summary><p>Yes. You send a redacted bill, not access to your systems. No API keys, no logins, no code needed for the teardown. You can sign a mutual NDA in one click. Files are used only for your teardown, never used to train models, never shared, and deleted within 7 days of delivery. If the work moves to a sprint, access is scoped in the SOW and removed at the end.</p></details>\n<details><summary>We're small. Is this worth it?</summary><p>If you spend under about $2,000 a month on AI, the dollar savings may be small. The teardown is still free, and the fixes that stop a runaway loop matter at any size. We will tell you straight if a sprint does not make sense for your spend.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Do you need access to our code or agent logs?</summary><p>Not for the teardown. The bill alone shows a lot. For the 5-Day Sprint, we work with read access to logs and traces and make changes by pull request, under a signed SOW.</p></details>\n<details><summary>What happens after the call?</summary><p>You get the video and estimate either way. If a next step makes sense, we send a short proposal: usually the 5-Day Sprint at $2,500 fixed. You decide. No pressure, no sales sequence. One follow-up email, then nothing unless you reply.</p></details>\n<details><summary>How does invoicing work?</summary><p>There is no checkout button. After the triage, if you want the sprint or retainer, we send a SOW. Once it is signed, we send a Stripe invoice. Pay by card or ACH. The sprint is invoiced once, before work starts. The retainer is billed monthly.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Which stacks do you work with?</summary><p>Claude and other Anthropic models, OpenAI, Cursor, AWS Bedrock, and custom agent stacks built on top of them.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Will the fixes hurt quality?</summary><p>The goal is the same output for less money. Every routing or model change is tested against your real tasks before it ships. If a cheaper model does worse, we do not switch it.</p></details>\n";
